Backport Baseband-guard to Linux 4.9: gate the "blk.h" include

kernel_compat.h unconditionally did:

    #include "blk.h"

That header only exists from v5.11, where it was split out of
<linux/blkdev.h>. On 4.9 the include does not resolve and the build
fails before anything else in Baseband-guard is even reached.

In 4.9, blkdev_get_by_dev()/blkdev_put() are still declared in
<linux/fs.h>, and <linux/blkdev.h> already pulls <linux/fs.h> in
transitively, so the existing `#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5,11,0)`
branch of this header compiles unchanged once the include is gated.

This is the ONLY 4.9 change Baseband-guard needs. The rest of the module
already has pre-5.x handling, verified against this tree:

  * security_add_hooks() takes 2 arguments below 4.11 --
    security_add_hooks_compat() already selects the 2-arg form there.
  * bprm_creds_for_exec does not exist before 5.8 -- baseband_guard.c
    already falls back to bprm_set_creds under `#if < 5.8`.
  * file_ioctl_compat is absent (4.9 has no compat ioctl hook) and
    disk_get_part is absent, so Baseband-guard's Makefile auto-detects
    both and leaves BB_HAS_IOCTL_COMPAT and BBG_COMPAT_HAS_BLOCK_DEVICE_API
    off, selecting the <5.11 blkdev path and the pre-3.18 gendisk
    partition-name resolution path.
  * DEFINE_LSM does not exist, so setup.sh's detection takes its SELinux
    route: struct bbg_cred_security_struct is appended to
    struct task_security_struct in objsec.h and tracing.h is linked into
    security/selinux/include/, with bbg_cred() resolving through
    cred->security.

Upstream: vc-teahouse/Baseband-guard @ a54e0dc6

--- a/kernel_compat.h
+++ b/kernel_compat.h
@@ -1,9 +1,21 @@
 #include <linux/blkdev.h>
 #include <linux/security.h>
 #include <linux/lsm_hooks.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
 #include "objsec.h"
+/*
+ * Backport for Linux 4.9 (LawRun CAF sdm845, 4.9.337).
+ *
+ * <linux/blk.h> only exists from v5.11 (split out of <linux/blkdev.h> by
+ * commit 2f0c5a3a0d0d "block: split out blkdev.h include"). In 4.9
+ * blkdev_get_by_dev()/blkdev_put() are still declared in <linux/fs.h>,
+ * which <linux/blkdev.h> already pulls in transitively here.
+ *
+ * So only include "blk.h" on the kernels that actually have it.
+ */
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 11, 0)
 #include "blk.h"
+#endif

 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5,11,0)
